      "term": "Cowl back",
      "definition": "An open back panel worked wider and longer than the front, with the extra fabric gathered at the side seams to create a loose draping pool of fabric at mid-back. The sides are seamed normally; the back itself hangs free."
    },
    {
      "slug": "treble-drape-g246",
      "term": "Treble drape",
      "definition": "Treble crochet used in the back panel instead of dc. The taller stitch creates a lighter, more fluid fabric that drapes well and forms the cowl pool without stiffening."
    }
